WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.470
[JOHN:] Good morning, Hank.
It's Tuesday.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:05.609
[HANK:] Good morning, John.
It's really… not my best work.

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:09.140
[J:] We very nearly had actual brothers
on a hotel bed.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:13.100
Hank, it's Question Tuesday, the day that we answer real
questions from real nerdfighters, and you are going to

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:18.150
have to figure out the theme of today's questions.
[H:] Oh, I like it. I didn't look. Okay.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.780
[J:] What, in your opinion,
is the most beautiful word?

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.800
[H:] I like “penumbra.”

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.660
[J:] For me, it's “ongoingness.”

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.520
[H:] I don't like “twelfth.”

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.260
[J:] That's a hard one.
[H:] Twelfth.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.920
[J:] What was the most foolish thing
you did as a child?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.180
[H:] I remember getting in a lot of trouble
for throwing glass bottles off of our fort.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.280
[J:] Hank, what do you think is the most beautiful
phenomenon in the Anthropocene?

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.480
[H:] I bet there's a couple colors that didn't
exist until we came around that are pretty good.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.960
[J:] I was gonna say the understanding
of the speed of light.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.160
[H:] That's good, too.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.120
[J:] Hank, what is your all-time favorite
foolish endeavor? I have an answer for this.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.079
My all-time favorite foolish endeavor is a
guy named Tony Hawks,

00:00:56.079 --> 00:01:01.539
hitchhiked around the circumference of Ireland
with a refrigerator to win a bet,

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:05.930
and the book that resulted is
as amazing as you would hope.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.000
[H:] That's a good foolish endeavor.
[J:] It is.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.320
[H:] I was just gonna say
all of humanity.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.920
[J:] Have you gotten the theme
of the video yet?

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:19.820
[H:] No.
I didn't yet. I didn't get the -

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.380
[J:] Are you serious?
[H:] No.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.240
[J:] You seriously don't have
the theme of the video?

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.720
[H:] No.
[J:] Okay.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.350
[H:] I wasn't paying a ton of attention.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.400
What was it?
Favorite word?

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.340
And then there was like...
stupidest thing you done?

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.680
[J:] Mhmm....

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.520
I think everybody out there
has the theme.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.520
[J:] This might get you to the theme.
[H:] Okay.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.900
[J:] What is foolish -
[H:] Oh, okay. I got it.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.200
[J:] Okay, finally!

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.300
What is foolish but also beautiful?

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.160
[H and J:] The internet.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.540
[J:] And also...

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.660
[H and J:] Humanity.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.380
[J:] Whaaaat.
[H:] And porcupines.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.880
[J:] We were like, in a lock step.
[H:] Yeah.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.820
[J:] The internet.
[H and J:] Humanity.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.880
[H:] Porcupines.
[J:] I didn't have that one.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.480
[H:] They're so beautiful.
[J:] I was gonna go, like, jalapeño poppers.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.960
What is the best advice you ever got
from your kid?

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.520
[H:] Sometimes Orin will say,
"Feel happy."

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.180
[J:] That's good. That's helpful.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.500
One time, one of my kids said,
“It's just YouTube.”

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.340
[HANK LAUGHS]

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.760
[J:] Are there any old school nerdfighterisms that
have made their way into your everyday language?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.840
In the very first vlogbrothers video ever,
the camera turns off and you say...

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.420
[PAST HANK:] “Auto power off”?
There's still some glitches to work out.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.750
[J:] And I say, “Auto power off, still some
glitches to work out” all the time.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.620
Like, every time something goes wrong with
the camera 13 years later, I'll still be like,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.980
“Auto power off,
still some glitches to work out.”

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.020
Is humanity worth saving?

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.420
[H:] Oh yeah.
[J:] Yes.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.320
[H:] I've thought about this
a bunch, actually.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.910
[J:] Right, it's sort of what you write about in your novels.
[H:] Yeah.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.040
[H:] I think super yes.
[J:] Yes.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.280
[H:] In fact, I will get into that conversation
fairly deeply in this book.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.040
[J:] Great, I can't wait.
[H:] I'm almost done.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.030
I will send it to you probably Monday.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:02.550
[J:] Have you stayed in any hotel rooms as good as
the one that had that Picasso since 2012?

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.620
[H:] I've never, nope.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:08.540
[J:] Not even close. We almost always stay
in Courtyard by Marriotts.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.280
[H:] Thank you. There's actually a courtyard
in this one, which is unusual.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.550
[J:] Hank, do you think that I should go back
to sports Twitter?

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.340
My Twitter account @sportswithjohn,
not regular Twitter?

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.620
[H:] I think you should do
what you want to do, John.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:27.720
[J:] Since I left Twitter, Liverpool Football
Club have not lost a game in the Premier League.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.440
So... why would I go back?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.680
[HANK LAUGHS]

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.000
[J:] I'm the one who's making it happen!

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.500
[J:] What's the last movie that made you cry?
[H:] It was the last movie I saw,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.260
which was Little Women,
which was very good.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:44.520
[J:] Every movie makes me cry. Like, I haven't
seen Cats yet, but I'm sure it will make me cry.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.600
[H:] I want to see Cats.
[J:] I don't.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.520
[HANK CLEARS THROAT]
[J:] But I support people who do.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.960
I'm not here to harsh on your yums.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.100
If you like Cats, whatever, that's great. God, thank God
that somebody likes something somewhere.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.160
[J:] Hank?
[H:] Mhmm?

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.160
[J:] I will see you, I will continue,
you know.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.160
[H:] Yeah.
[J:] Alright.

